+# Task 4 report — exact compatibility checkpoint passed
+
+The exact Linux amd64/Python 3.14 dependency combination passes two independent fresh uncached installations. `runtime/results/final-runtime-verification.command.json` records a fresh exit-0 verification of the retained actual resolver/validation outputs. This supports the Task 4 isolated compatibility checkpoint; Stage 1 readiness and Task 4 review remain root/owner gates. Temporary resource cleanup completed and was verified at 2026-10-06T00:51:14.960875+00:00 after retained-proof verification.
+
+Read Task 4 brief/Global Constraints, execution context and Task 3 report/review first. Task 3's final bounded source/evidence checkpoint passes both verdicts. SEC remained closed. This agent made no SEC requests, Azure resource/authentication commands, credential access or escalation requests. Root alone performed cloud execution. Work is confined to investigation runtime/evidence files and reviewed private temporary contexts; no staging/commits, workspace repair, production parser/worker implementation, publication, trigger activation or resource-profile comparison occurred. Original package deletions, plans, roadmap and other execution-time changes remain preserved.
+
+## Exact runtime and dependency proof
+
+Official Docker Hub Python `3.14.8-slim-bookworm` has registry index digest `sha256:c8137f4c460908c8763f281c8f22c431eb5c538514ba9553fc3a89c06b7cfb88` and Linux amd64 child `sha256:d1e795fbdab8a4744432467f32f348c6baa99f07abc05ffde710913f65c8261d`. Retained raw index/child/config hashes verify the publisher-provided digests and Linux/amd64 platform. The unpaginated returned tag inventory and ten public metadata bodies/receipts are retained under `runtime/public-metadata/`; root's metadata command/stdout/stderr record the actual retrieval. Docker bearer data remained in memory; final redirect queries/Location were redacted. No `docker buildx imagetools` success is claimed: the missing local Docker facility was handled by the explicitly accepted ACR exception and registry-protocol inspection.
+
+Actual successful resolver and both validation environments report Python 3.14.8, implementation ABI `cpython-314-x86_64-linux-gnu`, machine `x86_64`, Debian GNU/Linux 12 bookworm and glibc 2.36. Hash-pinned pip 26.2.1 is installed in each independent isolated venv. `base-image.json` records observed versions, registry/public pull authorization, exact index/child pins and rollback limitations; its earlier body is separately retained. This base image is not a built worker/release digest. No prior worker/release rollback image is established, and no image was pushed by these tasks.
+
+The five direct pins are Identity 1.26.0, Blob 12.31.0, Tables 12.7.0, Requests 2.34.2 and PyArrow 25.0.1. Current publisher metadata supplied exact Requests/PyArrow/pip selections; Azure versions are the documented candidates. Requests is synchronous and already needed by Azure core. The compatibility operation map requires no DFS-only ACL/path-rename/filesystem operation, so file-datalake is omitted. Final production per-object API/lifecycle selection is not certified by this map; any accepted DFS addition requires a new resolved/probed combination.
