+The actual resolver produced five direct and sixteen transitive pins, exact selected-wheel SHA-256 hashes/source URLs, Requires-Python and complete WHEEL/METADATA artifacts. `requirements.lock` SHA-256 is `523b2da36079ce4a7c6b11ac06feb0a7992a8c3aef757c32909850685023b5c2`. Binary-only resolution/download passed with no source build. Native selections include PyArrow 25.0.1 cp314/cp314/manylinux_2_28/x86_64, cryptography 50.0.2 cp311/abi3/manylinux_2_34/x86_64 and cffi 2.1.1 cp314/cp314/manylinux_2_17/x86_64. Azure core 1.41.0, MSAL 1.39.0, MSAL extensions 1.3.1 and all other transitives are fully locked, including yarl/multidict/propcache required by the selected Azure core. Downloaded wheel bytes remain ephemeral; their verified hashes, filenames, tags, metadata and public source URLs are retained.
+
+## Fresh execution and retained outcomes
+
+The accepted method used root-owned read-only COPY inputs at `/evidence`, UID 1000, an isolated writable venv and `/out`; no host bind occurred. Each actual SDK request explicitly set Linux amd64, CPU 2, timeout 1800, no cache and no push. Context allowlists contain only investigation inputs and hash-verified retained specimens, with no repository packages, Git, user/Azure configs, tokens or credentials. Hash checks verify successful inputs unchanged before/after execution. The brief's complete core probe is byte-identical in both validation contexts.
